\'93\'85we value the enthusiasm!\'94 the audience answered.\
\'93Oh, yes we do!\'94 Alexander sparkled at the camera. No one would deny he was a handsome son of a \'85 military conglomerate magnate mother (with all due fear and respect), but Eloise is for later in the story. Alexander gazed towards the back of the studio as if reading a faraway autocue. He beamed a smile, as if surprised by news. \'93The decision\'92s in, and it\'92s\'97\'94\
\'93Unanimous!\'94 The audience drowned Alexander out, as they always did.\
\'93There you have it, folks! Stay tuned for the sentencing. We\'92ll be right back after these important messages.\'94\
\'93Cut!\'94 the director called. Alexander went straight to make-up while an expectant carnival buzz pulsed around the studio.\
When recording resumed, Alexander parroted, \'93Thanks for those important messages from our sponsors.\'94 Turn to Camera 3. \'93Remember, for all your family planning needs, Pattinson\'92s Mobile Abortions, come to you, and take your worries away. Just call 1800-2229-4663. That\'92s 1800 BABY-GONE.\'94 \
Turn to Camera 1. Alexander whipped up the audience with, \'93And now it\'92s time for\'85 !\'94\
\'93The Wheel of Death!\'94 they responded. \'93Wheel\'85of\'85Death. Wheel\'85of\'85Death.\'94 \
A large, intentionally low-rent chocolate wheel was wheeled out by a pretty extra in an elaborate head-dress and swimsuit.\
\'93How lucky can you get?\'94 Alexander said. \'93Each episode, we put ten randomly generated sentences on the Wheel of Death. Let\'92s see which will be Hamish Hammersmith\'92s fate. Here are the options. Number 1: boiling in oil.\'94\
