\f1\i0 .\'93Get where?\'94\
\'93Wheels up in ten seconds,\'94 was all the answer he got.\
In the back of the police cruiser, Alexander was incensed. This was the second time today he\'92d been kidnapped by his own department. In the wee hours of the morning, the order came down for him to investigate a suicide. He hated investigative work. He was indolent about it; celebrity work was more entertaining and less work-like. He knew most of his colleagues despised him, assuming his good fortune had accrued only by the curation of his mother. So unfair! They\'92d rather envy him than credit his talent.\
He\'92d learned quickly he was assigned to such cases exactly because he was so lackadaisical. If word came down\'97possibly from as high up as the Commissioner\'97he was assigned to a suicide, then he knew to do the minimum to rationalise it as suicide, then go back to his studio make-up and A-list social life. As it turned out, the case was obviously suicide. Alexander found the weapon\'97a shotgun, would you believe?\'97with the deceased\'92s prints all over it. Now, with Alexander prints all over the case file, it would remain forever 
